---
name: tls-smoke
backends: [int, js]
known-red: "js — `tls(...)` emits a call to a definition the bundle never contains. `tls` is `RuntimeCall(tls)` and lives in the WsServer runtime chunk (js-runtime/ws-server.mjs:511), but `hasWsServer` (JsGen.scala:1444) triggers on WsConnection( WsRoom( serveAsync( sse( cors( and the http* client calls — NOT on `tls(`, so a program whose only chunk call is tls() gets `ReferenceError: tls is not defined`. v1/runtime/backend/js/BUGS.md `js-tls-intrinsic-missing-from-the-wsserver-capability-trigger`, diagnosed 2026-08-01 and handed to the ssc3-core claim, which holds JsGen.scala. NOT a new regression: `run-js` never shook, so the gap is old — it was hidden because the shaker used to DELETE the tls call, which 4f8c8cb9f correctly stopped doing. EXPIRES by itself: adding `tls(` to that list makes this lane pass and the suite then FAILS until this declaration is deleted."
---

# v1.5 Phase A — `tls(certPath, keyPath)` smoke test

```scalascript
// tls() builds a TlsContext value without reading the files.
// Actual TLS is exercised by serve(port, ctx); we just verify
// the primitive returns a valid value and the fields round-trip.
val ctx = tls("server.crt", "server.key")
println("created")

// serve() in headless/test mode skips binding; confirm it accepts a TlsContext.
// (Not invoked here to avoid blocking in the test runner.)
println("done")
```
